<Project>

  <!--
    Repo-wide build settings.

    TreatWarningsAsErrors enforces the zero-warning baseline that docs/ANALYZER-WARNINGS.md has
    documented up to now. SonarAnalyzer runs on every build, and without a gate the warnings rot
    until a real defect hides among them — which happened here once, a Split overload mis-binding
    in the metadata-folder guard that sat in a fully green build.

    Deliberate warnings and analyzer false positives are carried as targeted [SuppressMessage]
    attributes with written justifications, next to the code they describe. They are never handled
    by lowering this bar or by silencing a rule repo-wide: a suppression a reader can see and argue
    with is worth more than a severity setting nobody looks at.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
